/**
 * @file task7.cpp
 * @brief Implements functions to check the validity (tautology) of a Conjunctive Normal Form (CNF) formula.
 *
 * A CNF formula is a tautology if and only if every single clause contains a pair of complementary
 * literals (e.g., 'P' and '~P', or '1' and '-1').
 *
 * @page task7_page Task 7: Check CNF Validity
 * @ingroup task7_page
 * @details This module performs a structural check on CNF clauses to determine if the formula is a tautology.
 * Two functions are provided for integer-based CNF (from file) and string-based CNF (from conversion).
 * @subpage task8_page
 */

